        {
          "id": "SP_DUJARDINASCARIS_MADAGASCARIENSIS_CHABAUD_CABALLERO_1966",
          "name": "Dujardinascaris madagascariensis  Chabaud & Caballero, 1966",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Dujardinascaris",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Medium sized nematode. Males smaller than gravid females (average 59 % of their length). Cuticle transversally striated. Fixed specimens usually slightly coiled. Lips shield-shaped, with interlocking processes (Figs. 1 B, 3 B, C). Middle anterior edge of lips semicircular, with toothed oral plate, 21 – 23 teeth with slightly rounded tips (Fig. 3 C), highness and thickness of teeth 0.82 – 1.33 µm, 0.82 – 1.79 µm respectively; pulp of dorsal lip extended to the border of lip in four distinct lobes, and towards double papillae (Fig. 3 A). Pulps of subventral lips asymmetrical, main mass extending towards amphid and lateral papilla. Triangular interlabia well developed, reaching anteriorly to the middle of lip height (Fig. 3 B). Oesophagus slender, relatively long, terminating in minute oval ventriculus. Long anterior intestinal caecum present (Fig. 1 A). Nerve ring encircling oesophagus at approximately 13 – 20 % of its length (Fig. 1 A). Excretory pore approximately at level of nerve ring (Fig. 1 A). Deirids not observed. Cervical alae absent. Males (5 specimens): Length of body 10.2 – 13.1, maximum width 0.36 – 0.44 (Fig. 2 A). Ventriculus 0.099 – 0.113 long and 0.069 – 0.094 wide. Nerve ring and excretory pore approximately at the same distance from anterior extremity.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:8618061",
          "children": [],
          "uuid": "5f18884d-f884-5a7-b96-b7f4b081f10abb"
        },
        {
          "id": "SP_DUJARDINASCARIS_MAGNA_KHAN_BEGUM_1971",
          "name": "Dujardinascaris magna Khan & Begum, 1971",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
